WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:03.960
A department can have members, apparatus
and incidents in Resgrid

2
00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:06.340
and still have important setup gaps.

3
00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:10.489
The Setup Wizard gives the administrator a
repeatable way to identify

4
00:00:10.489 --> 00:00:14.369
those gaps, choose the modules the
department will use, and return

5
00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:16.079
to the right configuration screen.

6
00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:20.250
We are signed in as Wallace Boden in the
fictional Firehouse

7
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.780
fifty-one training department.

8
00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:25.129
Open Start or resume setup from the
dashboard.

9
00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:28.940
The nine steps organize the work from
department context

10
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.430
through review and handover.

11
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:35.000
The journey already shows findings needing
attention; we will keep those findings

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.880
visible while we configure the department.

13
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.290
Resgrid also supports resource and
logistics workflows for community

14
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.380
paramedicine and mental health response,
search and rescue, security

15
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.189
operations, wildland contractors, and
industrial emergency response teams.

16
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.659
The Chicago Fire names make this dataset
recognizable; they do not

17
00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:56.860
limit the system to fire and EMS.

18
00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.979
Begin with Welcome and goals.

19
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.510
Fresh setup is for a new department.

20
00:01:01.849 --> 00:01:05.319
Review existing setup is for an
established department that wants

21
00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.180
to check its current configuration.

22
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:11.699
Import or migration records that you are
bringing information from another system;

23
00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.150
it does not perform an import for you.

24
00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:18.439
The page groups features into core,
recommended, optional,

25
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.099
and paid add-on modules.

26
00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.210
Learning about a feature does not purchase
it, activate a provider, send a message,

27
00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:27.609
or change operational configuration.

28
00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:31.890
Every operational change happens on its
own screen, and you return to

29
00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.750
the wizard to verify the evidence.

30
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.630
Step two asks for department context.

31
00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:38.999
Open Department operating profile.

32
00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:43.010
Select the sectors the department serves;
our example chooses

33
00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.560
Fire, and EMS and ambulance.

34
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.379
Choose Career for workforce mix, enter
fourteen as the approximate member

35
00:01:50.379 --> 00:01:54.719
count, choose Central dispatch, and select
twenty-four-hour operation.

36
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.860
We also declare mutual aid and choose
English, captions and

37
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.200
plain language for planning.

38
00:02:00.649 --> 00:02:02.450
These are descriptive choices.

39
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.870
The member estimate does not replace the
actual roster or subscription count.

40
00:02:07.199 --> 00:02:10.149
Twenty-four-hour operation does not create
shifts.

41
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.370
A fire or EMS pack does not establish
anyone’s qualifications or clinical scope.

42
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.300
The profile helps Resgrid suggest
relevant modules to review.

43
00:02:19.679 --> 00:02:23.449
A mobile crisis team can choose Mental
health and mobile crisis; a

44
00:02:23.449 --> 00:02:27.210
search team can choose Search and rescue;
security and industrial

45
00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.239
teams have their own operating packs.

46
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:34.350
A wildland contractor can combine the Fire
context with a Contract workforce mix.

47
00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.589
Choose the context that actually describes
your department.

48
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.529
Click Save operating profile and look for
the saved confirmation.

49
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.479
Then use Return to setup and verify.

50
00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:47.730
That return link does not save an
unfinished form.

51
00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:52.230
This distinction matters throughout the
wizard: opening a screen, changing

52
00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:56.680
a value, saving the value, and proving its
behavior are separate steps.

53
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.809
After returning, the journey shows
Operating profile recorded.

54
00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:04.210
The department’s time zone comes from
Department Settings, which

55
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.690
we cover in the next tutorial.

56
00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:10.570
References to groups, policies and source
systems are also declarations;

57
00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.239
saving a reference does not prove an
external connection or

58
00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:15.789
that a policy has been approved.

59
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:21.340
In Choose your modules, use Use now for
modules you intend to configure, Learn

60
00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.090
later for modules you will revisit, or Not
applicable with an appropriate reason.

61
00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.409
Security checks always apply.

62
00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:34.040
Our example selects mapping, shifts,
training, contacts, records,

63
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.620
checklists, inventory, deployments and
automation for current setup.

64
00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:42.299
Changing the dropdown presents a Save
module choice button;

65
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.940
click it for that module.

66
00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.440
We save all twenty-one choices.

67
00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.760
The count tracks recorded decisions,
rather than successful configuration.

68
00:03:51.309 --> 00:03:55.039
Choosing Use now brings a module into the
wizard and report scope.

69
00:03:55.469 --> 00:03:59.370
It does not turn on a hidden feature or
grant access to a paid add-on.

70
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.270
People and access links to the roster,
stations and groups,

71
00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.540
roles, and department security.

72
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.549
Confirm the actual membership and who has
administrative authority

73
00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.480
before applying dispatch rules.

74
00:04:11.919 --> 00:04:15.219
Personnel roles describe operational
capabilities; they

75
00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:18.419
are different from department or group
administrator permissions.

76
00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.069
Dispatch essentials then links to the
call, unit and notification settings

77
00:04:23.069 --> 00:04:24.589
that control incident handling.

78
00:04:25.089 --> 00:04:29.110
Use the owning-screen links, save there,
and return to verify.

79
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.840
A feature’s learning checkbox records your
own understanding.

80
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.579
It is useful for training, but it does not
prove that a saved setting has propagated

81
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.969
or that an operational test passed.

82
00:04:40.119 --> 00:04:44.279
Your other modules shows the recommended
and optional modules you selected.

83
00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:49.369
Follow their prerequisites in order: a
stock workspace needs locations and

84
00:04:49.369 --> 00:04:53.809
items, a training assignment needs the
right participants, and a deployment

85
00:04:53.809 --> 00:04:55.649
needs its apparatus and roster.

86
00:04:56.149 --> 00:04:59.700
Plan and add-ons separates interest from
commercial access.

87
00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:03.430
Maintenance and workforce appear active
here because the isolated

88
00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.420
training stack uses a read-only billing
fixture with zero charges.

89
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.820
We choose Learn later for Push-to-Talk,
Advanced Data Protection and Enhanced AI.

90
00:05:13.269 --> 00:05:17.160
Those choices do not buy anything or
activate outside services.

91
00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.589
On your department, review the actual
plan, permissions, release

92
00:05:21.589 --> 00:05:25.620
availability and provider configuration
before relying on a module.

93
00:05:25.919 --> 00:05:28.749
Verify and practice opens the Setup
Report.

94
00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:33.130
Our recorded example has fifteen verified
checks out of twenty-three,

95
00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:36.480
with eight needing attention and two
critical findings.

96
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.819
The critical findings concern
administrator multi-factor authentication.

97
00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.840
Other findings include notification
preferences, communication

98
00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.360
verification, an empty group,
password-reset policy, overlapping

99
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.780
shifts and expiring qualifications.

100
00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.940
Read each finding and use its
owning-screen link.

101
00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.499
Unknown evidence is not a pass.

102
00:05:57.989 --> 00:06:01.839
Apps and devices, deployments, and
workforce have no automated

103
00:06:01.839 --> 00:06:05.079
checks in this report, so they still
require your own review.

104
00:06:05.579 --> 00:06:09.530
Passing configuration checks never
guarantees message delivery; a

105
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.800
communication test needs its own recipient
and channel review.

106
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.309
Step nine records administrative review
and follow-up.

107
00:06:16.779 --> 00:06:20.610
We choose October sixteenth, twenty
twenty-six, as the shared review

108
00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.880
date and click Save review date.

109
00:06:23.279 --> 00:06:25.470
The date is stored at noon U T C.

110
00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:30.320
A calendar reminder can be downloaded and
imported into a calendar; saving

111
00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.169
the date does not send a message.

112
00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.669
After reading the report, we mark this
report reviewed.

113
00:06:36.089 --> 00:06:39.460
The page records the review and its
evidence snapshot, while the

114
00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.390
eight findings still need attention.

115
00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.820
Reviewed means the administrator has
reviewed the report.

116
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.369
It does not make those findings pass or
establish operational readiness.

117
00:06:49.739 --> 00:06:53.290
Use the fresh printable report when
handing work to another officer.

118
00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.579
For your practice exercise, record the
operating profile, make one

119
00:06:57.579 --> 00:07:00.880
module choice, and follow one finding to
its owning screen.

120
00:07:01.269 --> 00:07:05.150
Save a deliberate change, return, and
select Verify again.

121
00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:08.769
Compare the current finding with the
earlier evidence and assign the

122
00:07:08.769 --> 00:07:10.940
next action to a responsible person.

123
00:07:11.339 --> 00:07:15.690
Keep outside systems and modules without
automated checks on the review list.

124
00:07:16.149 --> 00:07:20.259
This workflow solves a common department
problem: configuration decisions

125
00:07:20.259 --> 00:07:23.980
are spread across many screens and their
consequences can be forgotten.

126
00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.559
The wizard provides a consistent journey,
while the report keeps

127
00:07:27.559 --> 00:07:31.059
saved configuration, personal learning,
current evidence and

128
00:07:31.059 --> 00:07:33.099
administrative review understandable.

129
00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:37.980
Adapt the same exercise to a community
response team reviewing scheduled visits,

130
00:07:38.149 --> 00:07:42.259
a search team reviewing deployment
availability, a security company reviewing

131
00:07:42.259 --> 00:07:46.890
site coverage, a wildland contractor
reviewing seasonal crews, or an industrial

132
00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.829
team reviewing facility readiness.

133
00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:53.329
The software setup journey is shared; each
organization supplies its own

134
00:07:53.329 --> 00:07:55.509
procedures and responsible reviewers.

